---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import AiLandingHero from '../../components/AiLandingHero.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SolutionFaq from '../../components/SolutionFaq.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../../data/contact';

const context = 'AI for citizen access';
const mcpDocsHref = 'https://docs.registrystack.org/configure/breg-mcp/';
---

<Base
  title="AI assistants for citizen services | Registry Stack"
  description="People prepare a change to their details with an assistant you approve, using Model Context Protocol (MCP). They check and submit it on your official website."
  ogImagePath="/og-ai.png"
  ogImageAlt="Registry Stack: Design, adapt and access public services with AI."
>
  <SiteHeader current="ai-citizen-access" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <AiLandingHero
      eyebrow="AI for citizen services"
      heading="Let people update their details with help from an AI assistant."
      lead="People ask an assistant that you approve to prepare a change. Then the person checks the change and submits it on your official website. The assistant reads only the details you allow. It cannot submit a request, approve it or change a record."
      context={context}
      exampleHref="#correction-example"
      exampleLabel="See the change of address example"
      exampleNote="Fictional example: Alex’s assistant prepares a change of address. Alex checks it and submits it on the institution’s website."
      note="This assistant integration is a Preview. It works with a configured service on Base Registry Engine, which keeps your register’s records."
    >
      <div class="assistant-preview">
        <p class="ai-example-label">Example · Assistant from your AI provider</p>
        <p class="question-bubble">“Can I update my contact address?”</p>
        <p class="reply-bubble">“Your change is ready. Check it and submit it on the official website.”</p>
      </div>
      <p class="handoff-label"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span> Alex opens the link</p>
      <div class="review-preview">
        <div class="review-heading">
          <p class="ai-example-label">Your institution’s website</p>
          <span class="draft-label">Not submitted yet</span>
        </div>
        <p class="ai-example-title">Check your change of address</p>
        <dl class="address-fields">
          <div><dt>Current</dt><dd>6 Station Road</dd></div>
          <div><dt>New</dt><dd>18 Market Street</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="mock-submit">Submit change</p>
      </div>
    </AiLandingHero>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="correction-example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Change of address example</p><h2 id="example-title">Follow the path from a conversation to an official request.</h2><p>Alex has moved. An assistant helps Alex prepare the change. Alex checks it and submits it on the official website.</p></div>
        <figure class="ai-film"><video controls playsinline preload="none" width="1280" height="720" poster="/films/registry-stack-ai-film-poster.jpg" aria-describedby="film-note"><source src="/films/registry-stack-ai-film-720.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/films/registry-stack-ai-film-en.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" /></video><figcaption id="film-note">Fictional example: the film shows a change of address. It is 1 minute 25 seconds long. It has music and no speech. Optional captions explain each scene. The three steps below describe the same example in text. <a href="/films/registry-stack-ai-film-720.mp4">Download the film (MP4, 4.5 MB)</a>.</figcaption></figure>
        <ol class="approach-steps"><li><strong>The assistant prepares</strong><span>After Alex signs in, the assistant reads the details you allow from Alex’s own record. It prepares a draft change.</span></li><li><strong>Alex checks and submits</strong><span>Alex signs in on the official website. Alex compares the draft with the current record. Then Alex chooses whether to submit it.</span></li><li><strong>Your institution applies its rules</strong><span>Your register checks the request. Your staff review the cases you choose. If you enable this option, Alex can ask the assistant about progress.</span></li></ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="limits-title">The assistant prepares the request and the person submits it.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>What the assistant can do</h3>
            <p>The assistant can explain the service. It can read the details you allow from the signed-in person’s own record. It can prepare or edit a draft. It can give a link to the page where the person checks the draft. If you allow it, the assistant can also report the status of a request.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>What the assistant cannot do</h3>
            <p>The assistant cannot submit a request, approve it or change a record. The assistant’s connection has no tool to submit, cancel or apply a request.</p><p><a href="/products/base-registry/">Base Registry Engine</a> is the software that keeps your register’s records. It checks every assistant request it receives against the permissions you grant.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Who makes each decision</h3>
            <p>The person signs in on your official website. They compare the draft with the current record. They choose whether to submit it. Your rules decide what happens next, including any staff review.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="fit-title">Add an assistant for one task at a time.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Keep your website and front desk</h3>
            <p>People can still use your website and your front desk. People who do not use an assistant continue as they do today. The assistant is one more way to reach the same service under the same rules.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Choose the task and the details</h3>
            <p>You choose the task and the details it needs. You approve the details the assistant can read. You also approve the changes it can help prepare. Your register checks permission each time it receives a request.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Choose the assistant</h3>
            <p>You choose the assistant. The connection uses Model Context Protocol (MCP), an open standard. You can register one or more assistants that support MCP. They must also meet the sign-in requirements in the integration guide. They can come from one AI provider or several.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="section-note">For technical teams, the <a href={mcpDocsHref}>MCP integration guide</a> explains sign-in and the review website. It also covers the separate service that grants access to each draft. See how Registry Stack <a href="/architecture/headless/">connects to your existing interfaces</a> and how it <a href="/security/">handles access and accountability</a>. The connection is a Preview. The questions below explain what this means for compatibility.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <SolutionFaq
      heading="These questions come from data protection and security teams."
      items={[
        {
          q: 'What information does the assistant receive?',
          a: 'It receives the details you allow from the signed-in person’s own record. It also receives what the person types in the conversation. You write a statement of what the assistant will see. The service gives that statement to the assistant with the service description. The assistant provider handles the conversation under its own terms, outside Registry Stack. You should check those terms before you approve an assistant.',
        },
        {
          q: 'Which assistants can connect?',
          a: 'The assistants you register can connect. Each one supports Model Context Protocol (MCP). Each one signs people in through your identity provider. The service refuses requests from any other assistant.',
        },
        {
          q: 'What is recorded?',
          a: 'The connection between the assistant and your register logs each assistant action and its result. The log uses pseudonyms for people and assistants, not names. It does not contain the content of records. Base Registry Engine keeps its own record of each request.',
          link: { href: 'https://docs.registrystack.org/security/#an-ai-assistant-acting-for-a-citizen', label: 'Read the security model for an AI assistant acting for a citizen' },
        },
        {
          q: 'What does our institution provide?',
          a: 'Your identity provider signs people in. It must support token exchange. A service under your control grants and withdraws access to each draft. Your institution, a provider you appoint or we can operate the two connection services behind a TLS proxy. If we host and operate them, we quote that separately. You keep authority over sign-in and access decisions. We agree the connection work with you before implementation.',
        },
        {
          q: 'Does the service depend on an AI model?',
          a: 'No. Registry Stack contains no AI model. The service runs on its configured rules. The AI model is part of the assistant, and you choose the assistant. You can change or remove the assistant and the service continues to run.',
        },
        {
          q: 'Can our institution connect an assistant today?',
          a: 'Yes. The assistant tools and the review page are released and documented. They are a Preview. This means they are outside the compatibility promise. A minor release may change or remove an interface without a deprecation period. You should start with one task and agree with us when to connect real records.',
          link: { href: 'https://docs.registrystack.org/reference/api-stability/#experimental-surfaces', label: 'Read what the compatibility promise covers' },
        },
      ]}
    />

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 id="next-title">Choose a request that people can try.</h2>
        <p>Tell us which task people need help with and which details it needs. Tell us where people should check the draft. We then discuss with your team how to evaluate it.</p>
        <div class="section-links">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">See implementation and pricing</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .ai-film { margin: 0 0 28px; max-width: 880px; }
  .ai-film video { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; background: var(--registry-paper); border: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule); display: block; height: auto; width: 100%; }
  .ai-film figcaption a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .ai-film figcaption { font-size: var(--type-sm); line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 10px; }

  .assistant-preview, .review-preview {
    background: var(--registry-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule);
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 14px;
  }
  .question-bubble, .reply-bubble {
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--registry-ink);
    font-size: var(--type-body-sm);
    line-height: 1.45;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    width: fit-content;
  }
  .question-bubble { background: var(--registry-blue-tint); margin: 10px 0 8px auto; }
  .reply-bubble { background: var(--registry-paper); margin: 0; }
  .handoff-label {
    color: var(--registry-blue);
    font: 600 var(--type-xs)/1.5 var(--registry-mono);
    margin: 8px 0 8px 14px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .handoff-label span { margin-inline-end: 4px; }
  .review-preview { margin-inline-start: clamp(8px, 2vw, 24px); }
  .review-heading { align-items: baseline; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 10px; justify-content: space-between; }
  .draft-label {
    background: var(--registry-stamp-tint);
    color: var(--registry-stamp);
    font: 600 var(--type-xs)/1.5 var(--registry-mono);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .review-preview .ai-example-title { margin: 6px 0 12px; }
  .mock-submit {
    background: var(--registry-blue);
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--registry-white);
    font-size: var(--type-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    width: fit-content;
  }
  .address-fields {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-paper-rule);
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px 16px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 10px;
  }
  .address-fields dt { color: var(--registry-muted); font-size: var(--type-base); }
  .address-fields dd { color: var(--registry-ink); font-size: var(--type-body-sm); font-weight: 600; margin: 2px 0 0; }
</style>
